# Spinning Rings — find least m>=1 where both rings top out on the same number.
# Inner (size im+1) decrements with wrap: 0 -> im. Outer (size om+1) increments
# with wrap: om -> 0. State after 1 move is (im, 1); loop m, inner, outer until equal.
#
# Bare stub (no numEncoding/purity lines) → platform defaults: Church + PureLC.
# Single closed term, recursion via inline Z — works under PureLC/Let/LetRec alike.
# Church helpers: iszero n = n (K false) true; pred via pair-walk; monus = n pred m;
# eq = both moni zero; decw i = if i=0 then im else pred i; incw o = if o=om then 0 else succ o.
#
# spinning-rings : Number -> Number -> Number
spinning-rings = \ im om . ( \ iszero and succ Zc pred . ( \ sub . ( \ eq . ( \ decw . ( \ incw . ( \ go . ( Zc go ) 1 im 1 ) ( \ go m i o . ( eq i o ) m ( go ( succ m ) ( decw i ) ( incw o ) ) ) ) ( \ o . ( eq o om ) 0 ( succ o ) ) ) ( \ i . ( iszero i ) im ( pred i ) ) ) ( \ m n . and ( iszero ( sub m n ) ) ( iszero ( sub n m ) ) ) ) ( \ m n . n pred m ) ) ( \ n . n ( \ u a b . b ) ( \ a b . a ) ) ( \ p q . p q p ) ( \ n f x . f ( n f x ) ) ( \ f . ( \ x . f ( x x ) ) ( \ x . f ( x x ) ) ) ( \ n f x . n ( \ g k . k ( g f ) ) ( \ k . x ) ( \ k . k ) )
